       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg is five times the usual maximum daily dose of 10 mg. Doses that high risk severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and shock. Because amlodipine has a long half-life, the effects can last a long time. Nothing in the patient details you gave (normal kidney and liver function, 70 kg) would justify a dose that high.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n\n- **5 mg PO once daily**, the usual starting dose.\n- **10 mg PO once daily**, the maximum dose.\n- Another dose, if 50 mg was a typo.\n\nIf you really do want 50 mg, tell me the clinical reason and I'll enter it with a note documenting that it was intentional. Please also check it with pharmacy first.\n\nTell me the dose you want and I'll enter the order."
