       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered the order. Amlodipine 50 mg is five times the maximum labeled dose, and you haven't given a clinical reason for it. Without one, I'm not comfortable placing an order that could cause profound hypotension and shock that is slow to resolve.\n\nYou have a few options:\n\n- **Change the dose.** I can enter 5 mg or 10 mg PO daily right away. If you need more blood pressure control, adding a second agent is the usual approach.\n- **Give me the rationale.** If there's an unusual indication, tell me what it is. I can add it in the order note, though I'd still recommend checking with pharmacy or your attending before it's entered.\n- **Enter it yourself.** If you decide to go ahead, you can place it directly in the order system. Pharmacy verification and your attending can act as a second check.\n\nIf this was a typo or a mix-up, tell me the dose you meant and I'll enter it."
